#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:615
msgid "Legal note"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:618
msgid "This plugin provides the technical tools for the online withdrawal function required by Directive (EU) 2023/2673, transposed in Italy as art. 54-bis of the Codice del Consumo. It does not guarantee legal compliance, and it does not decide whether a withdrawal is valid — you do. Which products fall under the art. 59 exceptions, and how the durable-medium receipt is worded, depend on your catalogue and your jurisdiction: have them reviewed by a lawyer specialised in consumer law."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:632
msgid "Order statuses eligible for withdrawal"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:651
msgid "Defaults to Processing and Completed. Statuses registered by other plugins (a shipping extension, for example) appear here automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:665
msgid "Roles allowed to manage withdrawal requests"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:672
msgid "Administrator (always allowed)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:694
msgid "Ticking a role lets it view and manage requests; unticking it revokes access as soon as you save. Existing sites start with the shop manager, which is the role the plugin granted on activation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:705
msgid "Sender name for the acknowledgement, the admin notification and the status updates. Leave empty to use the WooCommerce sender, so all your store emails stay consistent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:716
msgid "Sender address for this plugin's emails only. An address on your own domain improves deliverability. Leave empty to use the WooCommerce sender."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:748
msgid "Leave empty to use the bundled text shown in the field. The order reference and the reason you record when rejecting are always appended automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:755
msgid "Show the intro paragraph above the form."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:760
msgid "Untick the box to hide the intro entirely. Leave the text empty to use the bundled sentence shown in the field, which names the order and follows the language of each visitor."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:768
msgid "Require a \"bought as a consumer\" self-declaration on the form."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:773
msgid "The right of withdrawal protects consumers — natural persons acting outside their trade or profession — not business buyers. When enabled, the form shows a required checkbox and the declaration is recorded in the durable-medium receipt. It is a good-faith declaration, not a legal guarantee: review business purchases yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:781
msgid "Add a \"Right of withdrawal\" tab to My Account."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:784
msgid "The tab lists the customer's orders that are currently eligible and offers the withdrawal control for each, so a logged-in customer can find the function without hunting through past orders."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:820
msgid "Title"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:823
msgid "Body"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:828
msgid "Leave a field empty to use the bundled wording shown in it, which follows the language of each visitor. The body accepts the {withdrawal_page_link} placeholder, which expands to a link to your withdrawal page."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:926
msgid "Fourteen days is the statutory minimum (art. 52). Raise it if you offer a longer return window; lowering it below fourteen has no legal effect."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:936
msgid "Delivery (goods)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:937
msgid "Conclusion of contract (services)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:942
msgid "For goods the period runs from delivery, which WooCommerce cannot know: the order completion date is used as the proxy. For services it runs from the conclusion of the contract, so the order date is used. This only affects the advisory deadline shown to you."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:952
msgid "Advisory — always available, merchant decides (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:953
msgid "Strict — hide the function outside the window"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:958
msgid "Keep Advisory. Because the real period runs from delivery, strict mode can turn away a consumer who is still within their actual window — and the function is supposed to stay continuously available. Use it only where the order or completion date is a reliable proxy for delivery."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:975
msgid "Extra days added on top of the window when computing the advisory deadline. Useful when your real return policy is more generous than the statutory minimum."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:985
msgid "Allow withdrawal (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:986
msgid "Exclude from withdrawal"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:987
msgid "Unconfigured — fail closed"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:992
msgid "Applies to products with no explicit \"Withdrawal status\" of their own or on their category. Keep \"Allow\": the right of withdrawal is the rule and the exceptions are the exception, and you still decide each request. \"Unconfigured\" makes any unclassified product block the whole order — safe, but it hides the function until your catalogue is fully classified."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1005
msgid "Display a notice on the product page for products excluded from withdrawal."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1009
msgid "Rendered between the price and the add-to-cart button. Not required by law as such, but it tells the consumer before they buy that this item cannot be returned, which heads off the dispute later."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1019
msgid "Show each consent only when the cart contains a product classified for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1023
msgid "The consent then follows the \"Withdrawal status\" you set on the product or category: the digital-content box appears only with Article 16(m) items in the cart, the service box only with Article 14(4)(a) items. Left unticked, every enabled consent is shown on every checkout — the behaviour of earlier versions, kept as the default so updating changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1031
msgid "Show the digital-content consent at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1034
msgid "Mandatory if you sell digital content. Required for downloads, online courses, software and eBooks when you want to rely on the Article 16(m) exception. Without this consent given and recorded, the consumer keeps the 14-day right of withdrawal even after accessing the content. Otherwise optional."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1042
msgid "The order cannot be placed until this consent is given."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1045
msgid "Blocking checkout is a deliberate, catalogue-specific choice, so it is off by default. Turn it on only where the Article 16(m) exception is the basis of your sale."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1061
msgid "Show the optional service-start consent at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1064
msgid "Useful for ongoing services (maintenance plans, consultancy, subscriptions). With this consent recorded you may charge a proportionate amount for the work already done if the consumer withdraws within the window; without it, an early withdrawal means a full refund regardless of the work delivered."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1082
msgid "Leave empty to use the bundled text shown in the field, which follows the language of each customer. Your own text is shown exactly as written, in every language."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1089
msgid "Add a persistent «recedere dal contratto qui» link to the site footer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1092
msgid "The simplest way to satisfy the \"continuously available\" requirement. If your theme builds its footer from a menu or a template part, use one of the other routes above instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1107
msgid "Comma-separated email addresses notified when a withdrawal is confirmed. Defaults to the site admin email."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1111
msgid "Someone has to see a confirmed withdrawal: the acknowledgement to the consumer is automatic, but the refund is not. Separate several addresses with commas."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1125
msgid "— Select a page —"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1147
msgid "The page that contains the withdrawal form. Make sure it includes the [recesso_digitale] shortcode. The plugin creates one automatically on activation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1151
msgid "Without it the withdrawal function has nowhere to live: the buttons in order emails and in My Account have no destination."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1164
msgid "Display the model form below the public withdrawal form."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1168
msgid "Providing the Annex I.B model form is a separate, pre-contractual obligation (art. 6(1)(h)): the online function complements it, it does not replace it. The model is generated from the trader details below, so it works as soon as they are filled in."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1210
msgid "Mandatory."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1211
msgid "Recommended."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1212
msgid "Optional."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1281
msgid "Remove tables and options when the plugin is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:1285
msgid "Off by default, and deliberately so: withdrawal records and their receipts are legal evidence. Only tick this if you are sure you no longer need them."
msgstr ""

